    {
      "slug": "reddit-upstairs-neighbor-noise",
      "script": "Who enjoys sleep deprivation? My upstairs neighbor played bass-heavy music at full volume past midnight for months. Management said, “just knock on his door.” So I learned he worked nights, then filed a noise complaint every afternoon between 9 a.m. and 5 p.m.—barking dog, vacuum, construction, anything vague enough to force a check. That meant knocking and waking him up, over and over, for weeks. He complained people kept disturbing his sleep. Management explained they were responding to resident complaints and had no way to verify who filed them. Bureaucracy found a hobby. Three weeks later, his music stopped at 9 p.m. sharp, every night. Apparently reciprocity has a volume knob. Who finally got a taste of their own noise?",
      "editor_note": "Punched up to a four-word question hook, 124-word pacing, one dry aside, and a specific question kicker; preserved every number and every shot phrase/query pairing."
    }
